{
  "dom_id": "question-133020",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $a=-\\frac{4}{5}.$ For what values of $k$ does the intermediate value theorem guarantee that $f(x)=k$ has a solution on the interval $x\\in [-5,-4]?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $k\\,\\in \\,[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$]$",
  "worked_solution": "In part 2, we found that the function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-5,-4]$ when $a=-\\frac{4}{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-5)$ and $f(-4).$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-5) & =(-5)^{2}+3(-5) \\\\  & =25-15 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nf(-4)=-5\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{5})=4,\n$$\n\nwe must have \n\n$$\nk\\in [4,10].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
